so login user and password should not be url parameters with 'params',
they should be form data in body with 'data'

in html form, GET method will use url parameters, 
POST method along with <form> element will use form data in body

URL parameters can be intercepted, particularly if they are used over unsecured HTTP connections
When data is transmitted over HTTP (as opposed to HTTPS), it is sent as plain text, 
which can be intercepted by anyone between the client and the server,
Always use HTTPS to encrypt data in transit. This ensures that URL parameters (and all other data 
sent between the client and server) are encrypted.
